To optimize performance, the program should process lines sequentially and minimize data copying. This can be achieved by reading each line from the file one at a time using `fgets()`, parsing the last two numeric fields from each line without copying them, and calculating the average for each line without storing the intermediate results in memory. The `getaddrinfo()` function can also be used to resolve the DNS hostname only once per line, which should reduce the amount of data being copied between buffers.

