This implementation uses a `POWER_REPORT_CACHE_T` structure to keep track of the RNTIs that have already been allocated and deallocated. It also uses a `RNTI_DB_T` structure to store all of the available RNTIs in the system. The `alloc_rnti()` function is used to allocate a new RNTI value from the database, while the `free_rnti()` function is used to free an RNTI value and add it back to the database.

The `populate_power_report_indications()` function populates the power report indications with RNTIs and CRC flags using the `alloc_rnti()` function. It also uses the `crc_flag()` function to generate a random CRC flag value for each power report indication.

