The function initializes each record's 'int' value with a random number within a specified range using the rand() function from the standard library. It also updates timestamps with the current time whenever a new record is added using the time(NULL) function from the standard library.

To handle concurrent access from multiple threads, we have used pthread mutex locks to synchronize the access to the linked list. This ensures that race conditions are prevented and thread safety is maintained.

The function also periodically prunes the linked list to maintain a maximum number of records, balancing memory usage against the need to retain historical data. This is done by iterating over the linked list and deleting the oldest record when the maximum number of records is reached.

