The function uses a mutex for synchronizing access to the log entries, ensuring thread safety without causing performance bottlenecks or data corruption. It also provides a mechanism for releasing allocated memory upon completion to prevent memory leaks. Additionally, the function is designed to handle both single-threaded and multi-threaded environments, with optimized performance for high-frequency usage.

