The function also implements a mechanism to handle memory allocation failures gracefully by using a backoff strategy that reduces the size of the allocated arrays until they can be allocated successfully. The backoff strategy involves waiting for a certain amount of time before trying again, which helps reduce contention and maximize throughput in concurrent access scenarios.

The function is thread-safe and supports dynamic resizing of the allocated arrays in response to changes in available memory. It also logs memory usage statistics at regular intervals using an external logging system, balancing the overhead of logging against the need for monitoring resource utilization."]

