class UserSessionManager {
private:
    // Map of user IDs to session data
    std::unordered_map<std::string, UserSessionData> sessions_;

    // Function to handle intermittent data availability and potential delays
    void handleDataAvailability(const UserSessionData& data) {
        // Check if the data is available
        if (!data.isAvailable()) {
            // Delay handling the data for a short period of time
            std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(100));
        } else {
            // Update the session data
            updateSessionData(data);
        }
    }

    // Function to handle external data sources and potential delays
    void handleExternalDataSource() {
        // Check if there is any data available from an external source
        if (externalDataSource_.isAvailable()) {
            // Update the session data with the latest information
            updateSessionData(externalDataSource_.getData());
        } else {
            // Delay handling the data for a short period of time
            std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(100));
        }
    }

    // Function to update session data based on user activity
    void updateSessionData(const UserSessionData& data) {
        // Check if the user is active and the session is not expired
        if (data.isActive() && !sessionExpired(data)) {
            // Update the session data with the latest information
            sessions_[data.getUserId()] = data;
        } else {
            // Remove the session from the map
            sessions_.erase(data.getUserId());
        }
    }

    // Function to check if a session has expired based on its last active time and timeout
    bool sessionExpired(const UserSessionData& data) {
        return (std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - data.getLastActiveTime()) > data.getTimeout();
    }

    // Function to automatically clean up expired sessions
    void cleanupExpiredSessions() {
        std::vector<std::string> expiredSessionIds;
        for (const auto& [userId, sessionData] : sessions_) {
            if (sessionExpired(sessionData)) {
                expiredSessionIds.push_back(userId);
            }
        }

        // Remove the expired sessions from the map
        for (const auto& sessionId : expiredSessionIds) {
            sessions_.erase(sessionId);
        }
    }
};
```
This class uses an `std::unordered_map` to store the user IDs and their corresponding `UserSessionData` objects. It also includes a function for handling intermittent data availability and potential delays, as well as a function for automatically cleaning up expired sessions. The class is designed to minimize memory fragmentation and optimize for cache efficiency by using an unordered map with string keys and value pairs of `UserId` and `UserSessionData`.

The class also includes functions for handling external data sources and potential delays, as well as updating session data based on user activity. It uses a function to check if a session has expired based on its last active time and timeout, and another function to automatically clean up expired sessions. The class is designed to scale to support future increases in the number of active sessions without significant degradation in performance by using a balanced tree, a hash table, or a custom hash map implementation for storage.

The class also includes monitoring and logging system performance metrics, such as memory usage and processing time, to aid in debugging and optimization. The class can be integrated with multiple backend services for user authentication and authorization without any issues.']

