The `dataCollection` struct is used to store a collection of data items. It contains three fields: `head`, which points to the first node in the linked list of nodes storing the data items; `tail`, which points to the last node in the linked list of nodes storing the data items; and `count`, which stores the number of data items stored in the collection.

