This implementation uses a linked list to store the `NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T` structures, with each node representing an entry in the list. The linked list is protected by a mutex and a semaphore, which ensures that concurrent access to the list is thread-safe.

The `init_crc_indication_list()` function initializes the list and sets its capacity to 10 entries.

The `destroy_crc_indication_list()` function frees the memory allocated for the linked list.

The `add_crc_indication()` function adds a new entry to the end of the linked list. It first acquires the mutex and then waits on the semaphore. If there is not enough space in the current capacity, it will reallocate the memory for the linked list with a larger capacity.

The `remove_crc_indication()` function removes an entry from the linked list based on its `rnti` field. It first acquires the mutex and then waits on the semaphore. If there are fewer than 1/4 of the entries in use, it will shrink the capacity of the linked list to reduce memory usage.

The `clear_crc_indication_list()` function clears all the entries in the linked list and resets its capacity to 10 entries. It first acquires the mutex and then waits on the semaphore.

This implementation of a linked list with thread-safe access uses a combination of mutexes, semaphores, and reallocation to ensure that concurrent access to the list is thread-safe while also minimizing memory usage.']

