In terms of performance, we evaluate the trade-offs between allocating memory in larger contiguous blocks versus smaller, more fragmented blocks to minimize fragmentation and optimize performance. We also consider the impact of using compare-and-swap (CAS) operations compared to simpler locking mechanisms, weighing their suitability for our application.

