The `performance_monitoring()` function monitors the performance metrics of the function by logging them to a file using the `fprintf()` function. It also includes a loop that runs indefinitely to ensure that the program continues running until the user stops it.

Note that this is just one example of how you could implement a thread-safe reference counting system, and there are many other ways to do so depending on your specific requirements.']

