The `validate_ip_address()` function uses a regular expression to validate the format of an IP address string. The `validate_timestamp()` function checks if the timestamp value is within a certain range (e.g., 1 hour ago) by comparing it to the current time.

The `calculate_average_payload_size()`, `calculate_packet_type_frequency()`, and `calculate_average_inter_packet_interval()` functions are used to calculate the average payload size, frequency of each packet type, and average inter-packet interval in a set of network packets, respectively. These functions return `-1` if there are fewer than 2 packets, or if there is no difference between the timestamps of the first and last packets in the array (i.e., the array only contains one packet).

