The `processSensorReadings()` function is responsible for processing the sensor readings in the buffer. It first optimizes cache locality for data access pattern by iterating through the buffers and checking if each sensor reading has a match with another sensor reading. If a temperature or timestamp difference is detected between two sensor readings, it logs a warning message to the standard error stream.

The `freeSensorReadings()` function frees the memory allocated for each sensor reading structure in the buffer, as well as the memory allocated for the SensorReadingBuffer array.

This implementation also uses the `rand()` function to generate random temperature values between 20 and 30 degrees Celsius. The `time(NULL)` function is used to generate timestamps that are approximately equal to the current system time in seconds.']

